target: internal/mutate/mutate.go
verify: go test ./internal/mutate/ -count=1 -run 'TestSymlinkTargetIsRefused'
expect: a tracked symlink target was accepted
why:    git tracks a symlink as a symlink, so a committed link passes the tracked-target check while the write follows it out of the repo — and in CI the catalog is editable by whoever opens the pull request
